ndia.indiatimes.com/science/in-1998-nasa-sent-a-rose-into-space-and-discovered-that-microgravity-could-change-its-scent/articleshow/133183735.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-12T19:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133183970,imgsize-144800.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Clavicular’s ‘I Can Fix Her’ Post: streamer hits on Ocasio-Cortez; congresswoman stays silent]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133186573.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Clavicular has reacted to reports about Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez’s split from Riley Roberts with a short message: “I can fix her.” The breakup was reportedly not recent and may have happened around two years ago. The comment comes after Ocasio-Cortez and Clavicular previously disagreed over looksmaxxing and its message to young men. She has not publicly responded to Clavicular so far.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/why-is-clavicular-targeting-alexandria-ocasio-cortez-after-riley-roberts-split-their-looksmaxxing-history-adds-another-twist/articleshow/133186573.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/why-is-clavicular-targeting-alexandria-ocasio-cortez-after-riley-roberts-split-their-looksmaxxing-history-adds-another-twist/articleshow/133186573.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-12T20:37:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sumit Roy</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133186573,imgsize-39415.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Dan Scavino, Natalie Harp, Walt Nauta: 3 aides were allowed with Trump when he wasmoved into a catering truck during Turkey emergency]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133186616.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/dan-scavino-natalie-harp-walt-nauta-3-aides-were-allowed-with-trump-when-he-wasmoved-into-a-catering-truck-during-turkey-emergency/articleshow/133186616.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/dan-scavino-natalie-harp-walt-nauta-3-aides-were-allowed-with-trump-when-he-wasmoved-into-a-catering-truck-during-turkey-emergency/articleshow/133186616.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-12T20:40:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133186632,imgsize-101384.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Florida's 23-acre Bannon Island, held by one family for roughly 150 years and reachable only by boat]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133184351.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Nestled near Haines City, Florida, Bannon Island—a coveted private island—has hit the market after remaining in one family for four generations. The residence skillfully marries aged 19th-century cypress wood with contemporary glass elements. With additional buildings and lush landscapes, the potential for creative development is endless. It offers the perfect balance of tranquility and accessibility, keeping Orlando and Tampa just a short distance away.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/floridas-23-acre-bannon-island-held-by-one-family-for-roughly-150-years-and-reachable-only-by-boat-helicopter-or-seaplane-is-listed-for-12-million/articleshow/133184351.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/floridas-23-acre-bannon-island-held-by-one-family-for-roughly-150-years-and-reachable-only-by-boat-helicopter-or-seaplane-is-listed-for-12-million/articleshow/133184351.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-12T20:32:41+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133186544,imgsize-1432155.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Minnesota funded $1.918 million for Shell Rock River habitat; 588 acres protected or restored by 2025]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133185961.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Shell Rock River Watershed initiative in Minnesota has made significant strides by securing 588 acres of critical habitat, surpassing its original objective by 105 acres through extensive restoration work. This program focused on acquiring various properties while bolstering wetlands and prairie habitats. Backed by funding for land purchases and aquatic enhancements, these projects are vital for the future of Minnesota's fish and wildlife.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2020-minnesota-funded-a-1-918-million-shell-rock-river-habitat-program-by-2025-it-had-protected-or-restored-588-acres/articleshow/133185961.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2020-minnesota-funded-a-1-918-million-shell-rock-river-habitat-program-by-2025-it-had-protected-or-restored-588-acres/articleshow/133185961.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-12T20:22:08+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133186128,imgsize-785088.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[20-year-old tourist dies in US after falling from 170-feet waterfall while posing for photos]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133186737.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/20-year-old-tourist-dies-in-us-after-falling-from-170-feet-waterfall-while-posing-for-photos/articleshow/133186737.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/20-year-old-tourist-dies-in-us-after-falling-from-170-feet-waterfall-while-posing-for-photos/articleshow/133186737.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-12T20:51:47+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133186820,imgsize-1348457.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California man’s HOA approved his food forest, then fined him $750 a year later]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133182540.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Chino resident has turned his front yard into a vibrant food forest for his family, but his initiative has sparked disputes with city code enforcement. Neighbors voiced worries about the garden's aesthetic and upkeep. The homeowner maintains he received approval from a prior homeowners association, underscoring the tension between personal gardening freedoms and municipal regulations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/california-mans-front-yard-food-forest-was-approved-by-his-hoa-a-new-board-later-fined-him-750-for-the-same-garden/articleshow/133182540.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/california-mans-front-yard-food-forest-was-approved-by-his-hoa-a-new-board-later-fined-him-750-for-the-same-garden/articleshow/133182540.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-12T17:52:17+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133182649,imgsize-298000.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Brazil’s R$20 tamarin nearly vanished; zoologist Devra Kleiman helped save it]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133182778.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Once teetering on the brink of extinction with just two hundred golden lion tamarins left, Brazil has witnessed a remarkable turnaround thanks to the efforts spearheaded by Devra Kleiman. Through a blend of captive breeding and dedicated habitat protection, these programs have successfully reintroduced captive-born tamarins into their natural forests. Today, the golden lion tamarin stands as a proud emblem of Brazil's unwavering dedication to endangered wildlife conservation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/the-golden-lion-tamarin-seen-on-a-r20-banknote-nearly-vanished-from-brazil-zoologist-devra-kleiman-helped-bring-it-back/articleshow/133182778.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/the-golden-lion-tamarin-seen-on-a-r20-banknote-nearly-vanished-from-brazil-zoologist-devra-kleiman-helped-bring-it-back/articleshow/133182778.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-12T18:40:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133183033,imgsize-168676.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Archeologists discovered 7,000-Year-Old Neolithic burial grounds in France]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133182953.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/archeologists-discovered-7000-year-old-neolithic-burial-grounds-in-france-using-electrical-surveys/artic